## Critical editing and synchronization logic

Do not simply add stock every time an existing working-sheet cell is edited.

This will create duplicate stock.

Instead:

1. Give every transaction a permanent unique ID.
2. When a transaction is created, register it in the ledger.
3. When an existing transaction is edited, update the original transaction or reverse its previous effect before applying the new effect.
4. When a transaction is deleted, cancel it or reverse its effect.
5. Recalculate stock from valid ledger transactions.
6. Prevent duplicate processing of the same source record.
7. Preserve an audit trail of all modifications.

Use transaction IDs and source references to make processing idempotent.

Use LockService around critical write operations.

For multi-step transactions, implement validation and rollback/error handling so partially completed operations cannot silently corrupt stock.

